            <ArticleTitle>Lhermitte's sign in thoracic spinal tumour. Personal observation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a case of midthoracic spinal metastasis with a partial transverse cord lesion a typical Lhermitte's sign was elicited by flexion of the head. This is a very rare phenomenon with thoracic spinal tumours.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
